## Strict Do's and Don'ts

### Do
- **Draw 1px solid black borders (`#000000`) on *every* card, button, text field, and mockup.** This is the load-bearing structure of the style.
- Use full-bleed muted brand colors as card backgrounds rather than as thin accents or text colors.
- Use Inter for all text below 24px and apply `-0.02em` tracking.
- Set card and button radii to `12px`. Escalate to `28–34px` only for hero-scale cards or phone frames.
- Use a cream background (`#f2f2f2`) as the main canvas.

### Don't
- **Do not add drop shadows or gradient elevations.** Use outlines and offset duplicate frames to show depth.
- Do not use muted brand colors for text, highlights, or lines.
- Do not use brand colors as text on white backgrounds.
- Do not write comments in the code.
- Do not let display headlines wrap before 4 words. Keep display sizes to 1-3 short lines.
- Don't use overused fonts (Arial, Inter, system defaults)
- Don't use gray text on colored backgrounds
- Don't use pure black/gray (always tint)
- Don't wrap everything in cards or nest cards inside cards
- Don't use bounce/elastic easing (feels dated)